.TH NOWAYPROMPT.CONF 5 2026-07-26 nowayprompt "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
nowayprompt.conf \- nowayprompt configuration format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I base/nowayprompt/config.ini
.br
.I base/wayprompt/config.ini
.P
where
.I base
is the first non-empty of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.IR $HOME/.config ,
and
.IR /etc .
.SH DESCRIPTION
nowayprompt reads at most one configuration file. It confines the lookup to a
single base directory:
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set and non-empty, otherwise
.I $HOME/.config
when
.I $HOME
is set and non-empty, otherwise
.IR /etc .
Within that base,
.I nowayprompt/config.ini
is the primary candidate and
.I wayprompt/config.ini
is the fallback; the first candidate that exists wins. An empty primary file
counts as existing and is loaded. The fallback is consulted silently, files
are never merged, candidates outside the selected base are never consulted,
and an existing file that cannot be read or parsed is reported as an error
instead of being skipped. An absent configuration file is not an error:
built-in defaults are used.
.P
The file format is the
.BR wayprompt (5)
INI dialect: assignments sorted into
.B [general]
and
.B [colours]
sections. General settings configure Wayland geometry and fonts. Colours use
0xRRGGBB or 0xRRGGBBAA values. Runtime labels, TTY names, and Wayland display
selection are supplied by the invoking command or Assuan protocol and are not
configuration-file keys.
.SH VARIABLES
Keys are hyphenated; underscore spellings (e.g.
.BR font_regular )
are unknown variables and make the file fail to parse. Values may be
wrapped in one pair of matching single or double quotes, which are
stripped along with the trailing semicolon.
.SS [general]
Integer (u16) settings, with wayprompt(5) defaults:
.BR vertical-padding " (10),"
.BR horizontal-padding " (15),"
.BR button-inner-padding " (5),"
.BR pin-square-size " (18),"
.BR pin-square-border " (1),"
.BR button-border " (1),"
.BR border " (2),"
.BR corner-radius " (10),"
.BR pin-square-amount " (16)."
.P
.B font-regular
and
.B font-large
(defaults
.BR "sans:size=14" ,
.BR "sans:size=20" )
take font descriptions: fcft/fontconfig-style patterns
.IR family [: attr = value ...].
The interpreted attribute is
.B size
(pixel size); unknown attributes are ignored.
.B font-regular
drives the description, error message and button labels;
.B font-large
drives title and prompt. Unresolved families fall back to the default
sans-serif and the bundled DejaVu Sans faces.
.SS [colours]
0xRRGGBB or 0xRRGGBBAA values:
.BR background ", " border ", " text ", " error-text ", "
.BR pin-background ", " pin-border ", " pin-square ", "
.BR ok-button ", " ok-button-border ", " ok-button-text ", "
.BR not-ok-button ", " not-ok-button-border ", " not-ok-button-text ", "
.BR cancel-button ", " cancel-button-border ", " cancel-button-text .
.P
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nowayprompt (1),
.BR pinentry-nowayprompt (1),
.BR wayprompt (5)
